  "notes": "{掃|は}く is a transitive verb ({他動詞|たどうし}) specifically for sweeping with a broom.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{掃|は}いている indicates sweeping is in progress.\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- [place]を{掃|は}く — to sweep [place]\n- [debris]を{掃|は}く — to sweep up [debris]\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {床|ゆか}を{掃|は}く (sweep the floor)\n- {庭|にわ}を{掃|は}く (sweep the garden)\n- {掃|は}き{掃除|そうじ} (sweeping)\n- {掃|は}き{出|だ}し{窓|まど} (sliding glass door - opens to swept area)\n\nDO NOT CONFUSE:\n- {掃|は}く (to sweep) — different from:\n- {履|は}く (to put on pants/shoes)\n- {吐|は}く (to vomit, exhale)\n\nAll three are read はく but have different kanji and meanings.\n\nRELATED WORD:\n{箒|ほうき} (broom)",
